  3. Why SQS + Firehose (Not Direct)

  Why SQS between API Gateway and Lambda?
  Without SQS:  API GW → Lambda directly
    Problem: Traffic spike → Lambda can't scale fast enough → 429 throttling

  With SQS:     API GW → SQS → Lambda
    SQS absorbs burst, Lambda consumes at its own pace
    Batch size + max concurrency = controlled processing

  Why Firehose between Lambda and S3?
  Without Firehose:  Lambda → S3 directly
    Problem: 1 record = 1 file = small file problem in data lake
    1000 events/min = 1000 tiny files = slow queries, high S3 API cost

  With Firehose:     Lambda → Firehose → S3
    Firehose buffers: flush at 2MB OR 120 seconds (whichever first)
    Batches hundreds of records into properly sized files
    Also adds partitioned folder structure: year/month/day/hour/

